@startuml workout_journal_production
actor User
participant Browser
participant "Frontend Cloud Run\nNext.js Pages Router" as Frontend
participant "Pages API proxy\n/api/*" as Proxy
participant "Backend Cloud Run\nExpress" as Backend
participant Supabase

== Login ==
User -> Browser : Enter email and password
Browser -> Frontend : POST /api/auth/login (same origin)
Frontend -> Proxy : Invoke allow-listed auth route
Proxy -> Backend : POST /auth/login
Backend -> Supabase : Auth signInWithPassword
Supabase --> Backend : Auth user
Backend --> Proxy : access token + Set-Cookie refreshToken
Proxy --> Frontend : Preserve status/body and Set-Cookie
Frontend --> Browser : Same-origin response
Browser -> Browser : Store access token

== Authenticated request and refresh ==
Browser -> Frontend : GET /api/notes/:date + Bearer token
Frontend -> Proxy : Invoke allow-listed notes route
Proxy -> Backend : GET /notes/:date + Bearer/Cookie
Backend --> Proxy : 401 expired access token
Proxy --> Browser : Preserve 401
Browser -> Frontend : POST /api/auth/refresh + refresh cookie
Frontend -> Proxy : Invoke allow-listed auth route
Proxy -> Backend : POST /auth/refresh + Cookie
Backend --> Proxy : New access token
Proxy --> Browser : Preserve response
Browser -> Frontend : Retry GET /api/notes/:date
Proxy -> Backend : Retry GET /notes/:date + new Bearer token
Backend -> Supabase : Read user-scoped note
Supabase --> Backend : Note data
Backend --> Browser : Response through Proxy and Frontend

== Logout ==
Browser -> Frontend : POST /api/auth/logout + refresh cookie
Proxy -> Backend : POST /auth/logout + Cookie
Backend --> Proxy : Set-Cookie deletion (Path=/api/auth)
Proxy --> Browser : Preserve deletion cookie
Browser -> Browser : Remove local access token

== Password recovery exception ==
Browser -> Frontend : POST /api/auth/forgot-password
Proxy -> Backend : POST /auth/forgot-password
Backend -> Supabase : Send reset email for Frontend /reset-password
Supabase --> Browser : Recovery redirect
Browser -> Supabase : Set recovery session and update password\n(public URL + publishable key only)

note over Browser,Backend
Normal application API and database traffic never calls the Backend directly from the browser.
Only the password-recovery password update uses the browser-visible Supabase Auth boundary.
end note
@enduml
